The `cmd = f"grep ..."` line is line 20, and `subprocess.check_output(cmd, shell=True...)` is line 21.

The `pattern` argument is placed inside single quotes in a shell command. A pattern containing `'` can break out of the quotes and inject arbitrary commands (CWE-78). `log_dir` is also interpolated unquoted into the same command, so spaces or shell metacharacters in the directory name can cause injection too.

